QUESTION 3 : What is the difference between Git and GitHub?
====================================================================

Interview Ready Answer

Git is a Distributed Version Control System (DVCS) installed on
the local machine. It tracks source code changes, maintains
version history, manages branches, and supports offline work.

GitHub is a cloud-based hosting platform for Git repositories.
It stores repositories online, enables collaboration, code
reviews, Pull Requests, and acts as a central backup.

Definition

Git
• Software
• Installed locally
• Version Control System
• Works offline

GitHub
• Cloud platform
• Hosts Git repositories
• Collaboration
• Pull Requests
• Backup

Important Keywords

• DVCS
• Local
• Cloud Platform
• Repository Hosting
• Collaboration

Memory Trick

Git = Manage

GitHub = Share

====================================================================
INTERVIEW TRAP
====================================================================

Q:
Can Git work without GitHub?

Answer:
Yes.

Git works completely on the local machine.
GitHub is only required for remote collaboration and repository hosting.

